
Chapter 10, Part 17: "Turn to Ash"

――This is bad.

Accompanying Emilia into the royal castle, Ram summed up the current situation with those few words.

First of all, Ram's own physical condition was bad.
As far as she could tell, this was the worst she had felt in the past year. Her body rarely felt truly well even at the best of times, so she usually maintained her performance by straining her willpower to its limit, forcibly locking her baseline state in place. ――That thread had slackened, and this gap was the result.

"It seems it was a mistake to go back to the mansion even once."

Having reunited with her sister in the Empire, she had rushed to bring the awakened Rem back to the mansion as quickly as possible. Impatient for results, she had hoped that doing so would provide clues to restoring her "memories."
Thanks to that, she was able to witness the long-awaited sight of Rem donning the Roswaal mansion's maid uniform, but Ram's own willpower had slackened as a result. This was the consequence.

At a time when the entire faction needed to unite to dispel the ridiculous suspicions cast upon Subaru, she found herself exposed, far from her best condition.

"――――"

Walking quietly down the long corridor, Ram observed the royal guards they passed along the way.
Just like the soldiers who had come to the royal guesthouse to fetch Emilia, their gazes and their entire bearing were taut with a sense of mission. After a silent salute, they let Ram and the others pass and saw them off with their eyes. ――However, once they had gone through, Ram could feel it in the air as the doors in the corridor were closed behind them.
Normally, it was customary to leave those doors open. The meaning of closing them was clear.

――This is bad.

The closing corridor doors, the atmosphere of the soldiers more strained than usual, and, above all, the escort of the Captain of the Royal Guard himself—all of it indicated the utmost caution. Which inevitably meant that, in the eyes of the other party, their impression had already veered heavily into the negative.
This, separate from Ram's own physical condition, was the reality of the second bad situation.

"...Somehow, I feel like we're being locked in, very politely."

"――I'm surprised. I didn't think even Lady Emilia possessed the sensitivity to perceive that."

Slowing her pace slightly, Emilia, walking beside her, murmured quietly. At her remark, which had keenly sensed the mood in the royal castle, Ram raised an eyebrow slightly and replied.
Hearing that, Emilia lowered her shapely eyebrows and said, "I guess so,"

"It feels like the air is all prickly, or something like that. Back when I lived in the forest with Pack, whenever I went to the nearby village, everyone would treat me like this... Maybe they're very, very scared of us."

"Indeed. It seems Barusu has messed up spectacularly."

"...I wonder if Subaru and Beatrice are alright. It sounds like Lady Crusch is with them too."

Shaking her amethyst eyes slightly, Emilia spoke those words, and Ram fell silent in response.
Frankly, the outlook was not good. From the information they had been given, the story was that Miklotov McMahon, a member of the "Council of Elders," had been murdered, with Crusch Karsten being pursued as the culprit and Subaru and Beatrice as her accomplices.

Because Ram had been bedridden due to poor health, she only knew the bare outlines of the trouble surrounding Crusch and the "Divine Dragon Church," but it was a plausible scenario: Crusch, cornered as a royal selection candidate, had committed a desperate crime, and Subaru, who happened to be present, had shielded her out of sympathy.

"For Lady Beatrice to be with him... no, she spoils Barusu too much, so it's no use. Barusu lacks self-control. He should only be thinking about Rem and... Lady Emilia."

It was a complicated feeling as an older sister, but she had to acknowledge that Subaru treasured Rem, and that had been a great source of comfort. Even Rem, whose "memories" hadn't returned, said various things with her mouth, but it was plainly obvious that she harbored special feelings for Subaru in her heart.
That was precisely why Subaru needed to tighten his own reins and narrow down the targets of his kindness. ――His people-pleasing ways had come back to haunt him, right now.

"Ram, are you angry, perhaps?"

"...I have always thought Barusu's fickle affections were incurable. But that's a separate matter from the suspicions cast on him now."

"Yes, you're right. We need to talk properly and make them understand Subaru. So we're ready for whatever they ask."

"For now, Lady Emilia, please prepare about ten of Barusu's good points."

"Huh, ten? I can only say ten? I wonder if I can narrow it down to just ten..."

As Emilia agonized over a completely different kind of worry, Ram was impressed that she could list as many as ten good points about Subaru. What else was there to praise besides his timing?

In any case――,

"――A critical moment."

Looking back, it felt like they were constantly facing critical moments, but putting aside such fruitless sentiment, Ram looked straight ahead with Emilia. ――There, Marcos, who had stopped, pushed open the door at the end of the corridor and gestured for them to enter.
Passing through the door as bidden, they were greeted by numerous gazes within the room and a tense, solemn atmosphere; Ram could feel the silent tension rising.

――The place Ram and Emilia were guided to was not the great hall, but a council chamber within the castle used for discussions among the castle's dignitaries.

It was the room where Emilia, accompanied by Felt, had previously attended the declaration of Felt's intention to participate in the royal selection and the nomination of her knight. It had been only a few days since that visit, but the treatment now was completely different, and the attitude of those around them was as if they were witnessing the escort of criminals.

"――――"

Looking at the room they were shown into, Ram first checked the positioning of the soldiers.
Two on either side of the door, four along the walls, and in the center of the room, surrounding an ebony round table in a semicircle, several figures could be seen standing in wait behind it.

All of them had their swords sheathed, not a hand on a hilt. ――Even so, it was clear that this situation had assumed the worst from the very beginning.

"A courteous invitation."

It had the form of politeness, but it was by no means a welcome.
It was the upper-class method of cornering someone, covering them with a fine box and elegantly denying any escape. As if to prove it, the sound of Marcos closing the door behind them overlapped doubly. ――The meaning of the two doors separating the room from the corridor was to ensure the conversation inside would not leak out.
But at this moment, Ram felt that it was for more than just ensuring privacy for the discussion in the council chamber; it felt like a more physical form of isolation.

"――Emilia!"

Just as Ram was assessing the room's atmosphere, a voice suddenly rang out from the person seated at the end of the round table――a woman in a nun's habit, characterized by her long golden hair and red eyes.
She kicked her chair back noisily, leaped over the round table without regard for the surrounding gazes, and flew straight into the chest of Emilia, who stood at the room's entrance.

Emilia caught her momentum head-on, blinking in surprise, and said,

"Felt, you came too."

"Of course! This is about Emilia and her knight, Subaru! I thought if something happened, I had to help, so I rushed here as fast as I could!"

"Felt..."

"It's alright! I'm with you! Well, I don't really understand what's going on, but there's no way Emilia is at fault! I'm on your side no matter what!"

Hearing the woman in the nun's habit cling to Emilia and say that――being called Felt, Ram recognized her as the new royal selection candidate who had played a part in the recent upheaval in the royal capital.

She had heard from Rem that Felt had become friends with Emilia, but this was considerable attachment. Her tearful red eyes and emotional demeanor, as if she were about to start sniffling, conveyed both genuine worry for Emilia and an air of uncertainty about how reliable she could be in this situation.

In fact, Felt's behavior was not welcomed by the others in the council chamber――the attending members of the "Council of Elders," several high-ranking nobles Ram also knew, and the royal guards.
As coughs and stern gazes rained down, the one who called out "Felt-chan?" was the woman sitting next to the seat Felt had kicked aside.

With a gentle tone and expression, she looked at Felt clinging to Emilia and said,

"Everyone is surprised, you know. You shouldn't frolic around like that, please."

"Frolic!? I'm not frolicking! I'm lamenting from the bottom of my heart! If I had stuck with Emilia, I could have been there for her unease from the very beginning! It says so in the scriptures too. 'One person's salvation is achieved through the prayers of all. When the dragon's blessings are shared with thy neighbor, the lonely soul shall find healing, and it shall become true salvation'!"

"The interpretation is up to you, but delaying the discussion won't make a good impression, you know? If Felt-chan fusses, won't it just end up disadvantaging Emilia-chan?"

"Ugh... Sakura, you idiot...!"

"Oh my, I seem to be disliked."

At Felt's tearful, childish retort, the woman called Sakura shrugged. It was an exchange with a clear difference in the performers' skills, but as Felt was being talked down, Emilia gently patted her head and said,

"Mm, thank you, Felt. That's very reassuring. Please watch over me."

"Emilia... Yes. Yes! I'll watch over you with wide-open eyes!"

"――Now, Lady Felt, please return to your seat."

Hearing Emilia's words, Felt, who had been roughly wiping her tear-filled eyes, nodded repeatedly. Then, as if seeing an opportunity to finally interject, Marcos urged her to sit down.
At his instruction, Felt reluctantly parted from Emilia, hurriedly returned the chair she had kicked over, sat down, and turned her face away from Sakura with a huff.

After that brief scene――,

"Lady Emilia, please proceed to the central seat. Your attendant――"

"Ram will stand behind Lady Emilia."

"――――"

"Is there a problem?"

"No, there is none. Then, please proceed there."

As a minimal act of resistance, Ram refused only to be separated from Emilia and stood by, diagonally behind Emilia as she was seated in the central witness chair. For a moment, their eyes met, and to those eyes holding both unease and gratitude, Ram responded with only a slight dip of her chin.

"Lady Emilia, we appreciate your making the effort to come here."

The one who spoke those solemn words was a bald old man with a particularly striking presence among those seated at the semi-circular round table――Bordeaux Zellgef.

He was a member of the "Council of Elders," which had seats prepared for seven, a hero of the Kingdom who had once wielded a halberd himself during the "Demi-Human War." He was also a figure known for his staunch stance against demi-humans born from that experience, making him arguably the worst possible match for Emilia.

His opening remark, outwardly showing verbal respect to Emilia while its substance was entirely different, might be an indication of that.
However, setting such circumstances aside, Emilia first fixed her gaze not on Bordeaux, but on the empty seat to his right, and said,

"That's where Mr. Miklotov usually sits, isn't it."

"――――"

"Is it true, about Mr. Miklotov?"

"It is a confirmed fact, without error. For the Kingdom, it is a loss greater than any other. One could say there has been no such catastrophe since the passing of the Royal Family."

Shaking his head slowly, Bordeaux answered in a hoarse, low voice.
Indeed, anyone in the Kingdom would have to nod in agreement with Bordeaux's answer, considering the role Miklotov had fulfilled for the Kingdom of Lugunica until now.

However, Emilia's reaction to that answer seemed different. She narrowed her eyes, framed by her long eyelashes, and said,

"...Is that all?"

"――What do you mean by that?"

"I understand it's a terrible thing for the Kingdom, of course. But Mr. Bordeaux and the others had known Mr. Miklotov for a long time, right? So then..."

"Do you think we should be stricken with grief and shedding tears? However, knowing Miklotov-dono, that is precisely what he would not wish for. He was not a man who would allow his own death to rot the brains of the Kingdom and cause its limbs to gradually necrotize."

"――――"

"Our ways of mourning our own differ from yours. That is all."

"...I see. I'm sorry. This must be very painful for Mr. Bordeaux and the others too."

At the sharp answer, Emilia let out a quiet sigh.
She backed down when told it was a difference in expressing grief, but Ram, watching from a step back, had a different impression from the kind-hearted Emilia.

Certainly, it was a plausible argument. If they were to carry on the will of a sage who always fretted over the Kingdom's future, there was no time to stand still.
But Ram questioned whether there was truly no room for mourning at all. ――At the very least, her misgivings about this situation, which was still unfolding, were only growing.

"Once again, the reason we have summoned Lady Emilia here――we wish to begin the inquiry regarding the suspicions that have arisen concerning the knight, Natsuki Subaru."

"The suspicions about Subaru, that's..."

"Yes. ――The suspicion is that the knight, Natsuki Subaru, is connected to the Witch's Cult, and furthermore, that he holds a position akin to a Sin Archbishop, bearing a significant role."

At the reiteration of the suspicion, delivered in Bordeaux's low yet penetrating voice, Ram frowned.
Personally, Ram thought it was a ridiculous suspicion, one the faction could do nothing but deny, but it was also a suspicion whose origin was unknown.

To be honest, Subaru did have the past circumstance of sheltering Spica, formerly the Sin Archbishop of "Gluttony," and there were many sore spots if investigated, but the Empire should have enforced a complete information blackout on that matter.
As they needed Spica's Authority, the Empire would not want her background to spread either. ――Therefore, it shouldn't have connected to the suspicions against Subaru.

"I can answer that question clearly. Subaru is not part of the Witch's Cult. Subaru is my one and only knight, an irreplaceable ally."

"That's right, that's right! Their bond is strong! I can also clearly... mumble mumble"

"Felt-chan? Let's be quiet for just a little bit, okay?"

Emilia answered the suspicion levelled at her with firm resolve, and Felt, who egged her on, had her mouth covered by Sakura beside her. But the result brought by both was the same――the atmosphere remained unmoved.
The cold heat residing in the gazes directed at Emilia, who had clearly denied the suspicion against Subaru, did not change, let alone for Felt's heckling defense.

Emilia likely sensed that too. Before the other party could speak next, she said, "May I ask something?"

"First, I want to know why Subaru is suspected of being in the Witch's Cult. I spoke with Mr. Marcos at the royal guesthouse, but Mr. Bordeaux and the others should know about Subaru's achievements so far. Regulus too, thanks to Subaru..."

"You refer to the subjugation of multiple Sin Archbishops and the Three Great Demon Beasts, the 'White Whale' and the 'Great Rabbit'? Regarding the 'Great Rabbit,' it is unconfirmed, but the rest are facts supported by third-party testimony."

"Right? And yet――"

"――However, those very achievements are the focus of the suspicion."

"――――"

The focus of the suspicion. At that spark of doubt placed at the heart of the topic, Emilia gasped.
It was an outrageous argument if ever there was one. To be told that the very achievements Subaru had made against the Witch's Cult were suspicious was unbearable.

"In short, you mean Barusu's accomplishments are too convenient?"

"I apologize, but the attendant has no right to speak. Please refrain."

"I overstepped. I couldn't help but doubt my ears."

A sharp glare intensified at her added, unnecessary remark, but it was Ram's true feeling.
Nevertheless, the other party must also understand that this argument was a false accusation――or at least, as things stood now, it was nothing more than mere conjecture. But since they were forcing this inquiry upon Emilia, they must have grounds beyond just this.

And those were――,

"Ram is sorry. But what do you mean by saying Subaru's hard work is suspicious?"

"The suspicion is that everything was orchestrated. That the subjugation of multiple Sin Archbishops, and even the subjugation of the Three Great Demon Beasts, were all part of a scheme to infiltrate deep into the Kingdom's interior."

"That's...!"

"Would you call it an outrageous argument? Yet, against the Witch's Cult, which has made nations taste bitter defeat time and again, too many results have been achieved in a mere year and a half. The same goes for the Three Great Demon Beasts. It is as if opportunities for the knight Natsuki Subaru to distinguish himself were intentionally provided."

As Emilia faltered for words, Bordeaux pressed on, piling those words upon her. As if riding the momentum of Bordeaux's statement, those filling the seats around the semi-circular table nodded one after another,

"The subjugation of the 'White Whale,' which even the great expedition failed to finish off, was achieved, and right after that, defeating that 'Sloth' Sin Archbishop... someone considered a calamity... it's too perfect."

"According to testimonies from those involved at the time, the knight Natsuki Subaru predicted the exact date and time of the 'White Whale's' appearance, and further preemptively thwarted the Witch's Cult's schemes one after another."

"I also heard that he completely suppressed that Sin Archbishop with almost no casualties. Considering the damage from incidents caused by the Witch's Cult so far, it's unbelievable."

"But, even for the Witch's Cult, would they sacrifice someone in an important position?"

"There's also talk that the Witch's Cult, especially the Sin Archbishops, hate each other. Could he have exploited internal conflict within the Witch's Cult at that time...?"

"――Wait!"

"――――"

As the waves of suspicion burst forth as if a dam had broken, Emilia's voice forcibly cut in.
These were likely statements the other party had been waiting for the opportunity to make, but all of them were weak as decisive proof of suspicion, lacking the power to make the seeds of doubt sprout.
Emilia understood that too. That was why, even as she was tossed by the rough waves, her trust in her knight, dwelling in her eyes, didn't waver in the slightest.

"All of those things you just said, it just seems to me like you already decided Subaru was suspicious beforehand, and that's why you see it that way. It's true, Subaru has very good intuition, he always finds the very best way, and thanks to that we've managed against the Witch's Cult..."

"That argument might be counterproductive..."

"But! Don't just look at my knight only in relation to the Witch's Cult and the Three Great Demon Beasts! At the Pleiades Watchtower, in Vollachia too... no, that's not right. Even before that, right here in the royal capital, when I was in danger, Subaru saved me. Completely unrelated to the Witch's Cult!"

"Lady Emilia..."

Ram's eyes widened slightly at Emilia's flushed cheeks and desperate appeal.
Emilia's rebuttal, though undeniably clumsy in phrasing, directly confronted the suspicions Bordeaux and the others had raised.

Even Ram only rated Subaru's good timing, but the situations where that was demonstrated weren't limited to those related to the Witch's Cult. In a manner of speaking, Subaru always had good timing. That suspiciousness was not equal to the suspicion that he was a member of the Witch's Cult.

Therefore――,

"――We understand what Lady Emilia is trying to say. We, too, have no intention of besmirching the honor of the knight Natsuki Subaru with what amounts to mere false accusations."

"...Really? Then that's good. So..."

"――However, strong suspicion falls upon your knight as a successor to the Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth.' What do you have to say about this?"

In the end, this was all just a preliminary skirmish, Ram realized, grinding her back teeth.




















---------








――The succession of the Sin Archbishop of "Sloth"—that was the main suspicion cast upon Natsuki Subaru.

At this question, which came from completely outside her expectations, Emilia's amethyst eyes wavered greatly. Meanwhile, hearing it behind her, Ram also deepened the confusion in her pale pink eyes.

"From what I've heard, the Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth' was killed by Barusu and Otto."

Hearing Ram's understanding of it, she could almost imagine Otto saying, "I'd like to object to that statement!", but right now she had no ear to lend to the absent straight-man. 
However, although she wasn't directly involved, Ram had indirectly taken part in the battle against the Sin Archbishop of "Sloth." That person, the most infamous Sin Archbishop in the world, died, and it undoubtedly marked the beginning of the Emilia faction's fated conflict with the Witch's Cult. 
But why was Subaru's connection to that Sin Archbishop of "Sloth" being suspected—?

"Is that also because Barusu conveniently distinguished himself in subjugating 'Sloth'?"

"You have no right to—"

"No, let her speak. That is part of it. But the greatest focus lies on a certain testimony."

"Testimony?"

Taking over for Emilia, whose thoughts seemed to have stalled, Ram pressed for the continuation. Marcos moved to admonish her, but Bordeaux held him back with a hand and revealed the rest.
The greatest focus of the suspicion against Subaru was—,

"—The testimony of the captured Sin Archbishop of 'Wrath'."

"—Tch, Sirius!"

"That Sin Archbishop is currently held captive in the prison tower. She has not responded properly to our interrogations, but it is said she has spoken several times, including during her transport from the Water Gate City. —She stated that the Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth' resides within Natsuki Subaru."

"——"

"I also recall the detailed report given during the commendation ceremony held in the royal capital... when the achievements of subjugating the 'White Whale' and the Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth' were honored. Within it was the fact that the Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth' was an evil spirit that possessed the bodies of others, migrating through numerous vessels. —What say you to that?"

At Bordeaux's question, narrowing his eyes beneath his thick eyebrows, Emilia's cheeks tensed.
It wasn't that suspicion of Subaru had arisen within her. Rather, at this terrible confluence of factors working against Subaru, her overflowing emotions simply couldn't find words.

In short, what they were suggesting was that Natsuki Subaru's body had been taken over by the Sin Archbishop of "Sloth," and from that day to this, he had been merely a role played by someone else.

That was surely an unbearable insult to Emilia, who had welcomed Subaru as her knight.
Above all, that suspicion was, for Ram as well—,

"—This is completely beneath discussion."

Ram only realized her voice had become sharp, laced with danger, upon hearing the words she'd spoken aloud.
However, even aware of that fact, she could not suppress the emotion welling up in her next words. —Because that suspicion of Subaru, that insult, was equivalent to concluding that even Subaru's devoted nightly visits to the still-sleeping Rem had been nothing but a deliberate act.

"I cannot believe that the esteemed members of the 'Council of Elders' would hold such a session based on that kind of suspicion. Before the content of the suspicion, the source of the information itself is the problem."

"Then are you saying this matter is completely groundless, nothing more than our own petty conjecture?"

"Naturally. It is madness to believe the words of a Sin Archbishop. The captured 'Wrath' supposedly had the power to influence the hearts of others. Perhaps through that effect—"

"—Ram!"

In an instant, cold water was thrown on her heated consciousness, and Ram choked her breath.
Looking, she saw Emilia had risen from the witness seat, turning back towards her. Her perfectly beautiful features were sharp with anger—feigning anger—directed at her insolent attendant. Ram's heart was filled with self-reproach, both for making Emilia put on such an inept act and for allowing herself to become so emotional that Emilia had to rebuke her.
This is bad. —The lack of physical leeway was adversely affecting her emotions. What had she volunteered to accompany Emilia for?

"I'm sorry again, Ram. If necessary, I will order you to leave."

With Ram reflecting on her own actions behind her, Emilia turned back to the semi-circular table and made that declaration.
That uncharacteristically stern tone was Emilia's own way of covering for Ram's mistake. Having the responsibility for her own actions taken up by her mistress only intensified Ram's frustration.
Emilia's growth was a joyful thing. If only it weren't under these circumstances. —If only it weren't in a place like this, a hearing where the conclusion was already decided.

"—. There should be no need for you to leave. Refrain from speaking further. If you continue, it is Lady Emilia's own standing that will be called into question."

"...I will take that to heart. My apologies."

While voicing her apology, Ram couldn't help but taste bitterness at the fact that she wasn't ordered to leave, as it confirmed her own conjecture.
She felt there was an intention to keep Emilia and Ram collectively together in this place.

"Thank you for not making Ram leave. ...Then let me ask as well. Do you truly think Subaru might be the Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth,' just because Sirius said so?"

"Naturally, it was initially dismissed as nonsense. Taking the words of a captive Sin Archbishop seriously would be the more foolish act. However, Miklotov-dono was not like that. He was a man with the insight to distinguish between delusions that should be ignored and omens of disaster that should not."

"Mr. Miklotov did... Ah, then, could it be..."

As Emilia involuntarily brought a hand to her mouth, Ram arrived at the same thought.
Today, after preparing to depart for Priestella, Subaru had taken Beatrice along and left for an appointment with Miklotov, claiming he had a secret matter to discuss. What happened after that isn't known in detail, but there's no doubt it led to the bloodshed and the current situation.
Perhaps the very reason Miklotov summoned Subaru was—,

"The detailed purpose of that meeting wasn't shared even with us. However, considering that the knight Natsuki Subaru was present, along with Duke Karsten, who cooperated in the subjugation of the 'White Whale' and the subsequent battle against 'Sloth,' we are forced to harbor this suspicion. —That something inconvenient for knight Natsuki Subaru occurred, and Miklotov-dono was killed for it."

"That is—"

"Then how are we supposed to trust someone who has abandoned their own chance to explain themselves!?"

"—!"

In an instant, Bordeaux's thunderous roar exploded, and Emilia, struck head-on by it, stiffened.
Behind Emilia's reaction, Ram also felt resentment — at the terrible confluence of events, or rather, at the situation itself, which felt deliberately orchestrated.
As expected, the opposing side had solidified arguments that couldn't be refuted before summoning Emilia.

"Our worst fears were right on the mark."

From the sequence of events since they were approached at the royal guesthouse, it was the worst-case scenario that at least Ram and Otto had envisioned there — a summons to the castle that couldn't be refused, coupled with the division of their faction.
Whoever sketched out this picture had meticulously spun their threads this far.

Still, Bordeaux's pursuit continued.

"From the scene of Miklotov-dono's murder, knight Natsuki Subaru fled together with Duke Karsten. According to the testimony of those present, knight Natsuki Subaru used an inexplicable art, negated the magic of others, and manipulated an invisible 'something.' This is also according to reports received during our deliberations, but the Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth' supposedly wielded invisible arms."

"That was magic devised by Subaru and Beatrice..."

"Furthermore, asking around, victims of the Sin Archbishop of 'Gluttony' suffer the loss of their existence from the memories of others, or conversely, may even lose their own memories. Yet there are accounts that knight Natsuki Subaru remembered those who were forgotten. Why is that?"

"It's because Subaru remembered them that both Rem and Julius were spared from being left all alone!"

"Due to the atrocities of the Sin Archbishop of 'Lust,' Duke Karsten suffered incurable wounds. How do you explain that knight Natsuki Subaru escaped unharmed despite being subjected to the same affliction? Can you?"

"That's exactly what Subaru regretted most!"

"Then, where did knight Natsuki Subaru come from, and what exactly is he!? There are no records of him anywhere before he announced his candidacy as your knight in the royal castle! Why is that!?"

"Subaru is—!"

"—Stop it, please!!"

Battered by the storm of questions, her very answers cut off midway, Emilia was about to cry out in a voice so anguished it seemed she might weep. —In that instant, what resounded through the council chamber, overpowering her, was Felt, who had stood up from her seat at the edge of the room and slammed her hand on the semi-circular table.

A single tear streaming from her crimson eyes, her lips trembling, she declared,

"Don't all of you gang up on Emilia like this... She's the one who's most confused, and she's the one who wants to talk to Subaru more than anyone."

"...We are not raising our voices harshly without necessity. Above all, it should have been a colleague of Lady Felt from the 'Divine Dragon Church' who recovered Miklotov-dono's remains and provided the details of what happened at his estate."

"I know that! About Teiga being injured, too... but couldn't it be that Teiga, who had lost so much blood, just carelessly saw something wrong?"

"As expected, that's a bit too unfair to Teiga-chan, you know?"

"—In any case! I'm against this kind of method! It says so in the scriptures too! 'There is not a single soul without salvation under this sky. If you look up to the heavens, there is always the dragon's shadow, and there, equal salvation is promised to all its children'!"

Invoking the scriptures, Felt virtually slammed them down on the semi-circular table.
Her emotional rebuttal threw water on the proceedings, but the disadvantageous situation for Subaru remained unchanged. And what Ram feared was the further accusations that would accompany this suspicion against Subaru.
That was—,

"—I must ask whether Lady Emilia, her backer Margrave Roswaal L. Mathers, and the faction were aware of this matter."

"——"

"If this was colluded upon and concealed within the faction, then supposing the suspicion that knight Natsuki Subaru is the successor to the Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth' were true, the very reason for Lady Emilia's participation in the royal selection and the accumulation of achievements up to today would also..."

Everything that had been built up since the start of the royal selection — the results of all the efforts of Emilia, of Subaru, of the faction — would be declared fabricated falsehoods.
Everything they had all built with their blood, sweat, and tears, all of it—,

"—Emilia?"

Suddenly, a foolish voice struck Ram's ear as she clenched her fist tightly.
It came from Felt, still in the posture of pressing her scriptures against the table, her eyes opened wide and round. She blinked her large eyes, staring blankly at the center of the room.
Drawn by that, Ram also looked there, at the witness stand. —She looked at Emilia standing there.

She had been told things that would make it no wonder if everything went dark before her eyes.
She had been slammed with a despair that could make the ground crumble beneath her feet and lose all sense of where she stood.
Swept away by a storm of unreason and absurdity, it wouldn't have been strange for her to burst into tears and wail.

But—,

"—My name is Emilia. Just Emilia. The 'Frozen Witch' of the Elior Great Forest."

Standing at the witness stand, Emilia declared this, raising a pointed finger towards the sky.
It was a pose Ram had seen many times before—the posture of a recklessly daring boy when he was about to say and start the most foolish thing in the world.

"It's not the first time I've been looked at with those eyes of yours. I've been on the receiving end of those looks many times now. I'd get depressed, then give a great big heave-ho and lift my face back up."

"——"

"That's why I'm perfectly fine with going right back to square one. I—we won't lose."

"Lady... Emilia..."

"We won't lose. —Isn't that right, Ram!"

Still pointing her finger toward the sky, without looking back, Emilia called out to her.
The fact that she didn't turn around to confirm was, infuriatingly, nothing less than proof of trust. Emilia had complete faith in whatever Ram would retort, and in whatever face Ram was making.
That was why. That was why she didn't turn around. Ram had to live up to that trust.

She had volunteered herself to accompany Emilia.
Pushing aside everyone else who wanted to answer Emilia's trust here, Ram herself had done it, by her own choice.

"—Hah! Naturally."

To that trust, Ram matched her own expression, her voice.
Bravely and with dignity, spirited and gallant, embodying the "Ram" that Emilia believed in—so that she could support Emilia from behind, as she gritted her teeth and declared she would not lose, no matter the hardship.

"Look closely, you fools."

There was no way this Emilia could have been forged by walking a path moderately paved with promised, deceitful achievements.

Fools who harbor doubts—may you all burn and turn to ash.
Shall I gouge out those eyes that idly suspect this of being fake and stuff glass beads in their place?

Because this brilliance, forged through tears, wails, blood, and sweat, was the very vessel of kingship that Emilia had truly won through her own desperate effort.

"——"

No one could immediately respond.
Mockery, suspicion, plausible-sounding arguments—all of them, just for that moment, lost their place before Emilia's declaration of self.

"—Message! A message!"

The silence, heated and dominating the council chamber following the out-of-place declarations made by the master-servant pair of Emilia and Ram, was shattered by the voice of a soldier rushing in.
Marcos, who had been standing by near the entrance observing the inquiry, blocked the soldier who had burst in and roared, "Fool!"

"We are in the middle of an important inquiry! What are you thinking!?"

"My apologies! But there is something that must be reported immediately!"

"Immediately? What is it?"

At the soldier's appeal, colored with agitation, Marcos turned half his body and lent an ear. Then, upon hearing the soldier's lowered voice, deep wrinkles carved themselves into Marcos's brow, and a heavy murmur of "I see" leaked out.
Hearing a note akin to understanding in that murmur, Ram narrowed her eyes.
Thereupon—,

"Captain Marcos, what has happened? Does it concern the inquiry?"

At Bordeaux's question, Marcos turned, glancing briefly towards Emilia. Then, the head atop his enormous frame slowly shook from side to side.

"It is not unrelated."

"Then let us hear it. The soldier's fluster suggests it is no trivial matter."

"—The members of Lady Emilia's faction who remained at the royal guesthouse took advantage of a gap in the surveillance and left the premises. There are no injuries among the soldiers who moved to stop them, but we are currently pursuing their whereabouts."

"What...!"

Upon Marcos's low, delivered report, Bordeaux brought a hand to his mouth. Then, the gaunt elder sage let out a sigh as if in lamentation and stared at Emilia.

"While the master offers explanations at the royal castle, her subordinates have resorted to deceiving the Kingdom's eyes behind her back. To take this in a favorable light is, to say the least, somewhat unreasonable."

"I don't think that's true. If everyone did that, it means everyone thought that was the best thing to do."

"Regrettably, that answer is far from convincing. —Lady Emilia, including the suspicions regarding knight Natsuki Subaru, we must ask you to remain within the castle."

As Bordeaux gave that order, feigning regret with words alone, Ram gritted her teeth.
That man's hatred of demi-humans was well-known, but it was hard to believe he would so forcefully move to eliminate Emilia just because Miklotov, seen as a moderate, was gone.
This deft maneuvering—perhaps even Miklotov's death itself... in any case, that attitude of feigned regret was nothing but transparently insincere.

After all, it must have been decided from the very beginning that this inquiry would conclude this way.
That was precisely why—,

"—Rem, make sure to give Garf and Otto a good kick in the rear. We're counting on you."

It was a parting they had accepted with resolve, knowing there was no choice but to entrust the roles that the detained and immobilized Emilia and Ram could not fulfill to Rem and the others they had left behind.






