"—Emilia-neechan!"

"Felt-chan?"

They were in the midst of being escorted out of the council chamber where the inquiry had been held and moved to a separate room within the castle.
The one who came running up to Emilia with pattering footsteps, her expression desperate, was one of her fellow royal selection candidates, Felt.

Felt, having rushed up in front of Emilia, glared in turn at the royal soldiers standing so as to box Emilia in from front and back.

"Oi, what's the big idea here? This's like treatin' neechan like some kinda criminal. We're royal selection candidates, y'know. You really think you can get away with this crap?"

"Felt-chan, it's alright! I've accepted... well, I haven't really accepted it at all, but I've done something sort of like accepting it."

"The hell's that supposed to mean! There ain't no sorta-kinda about accepting! It's either you do or you don't! If you haven't, then you haven't!"

At Felt's fierce, undisguised anger, Emilia's eyes widened, and then her brow lowered sadly. Felt was angry on her behalf—and that made Emilia happy.
She was seized by an urge to hug her, but if she did, they might think she was trying to take Felt hostage, so she held back tightly.

"Lady Felt, your feelings are most appreciated. However, please rest assured that Lady Emilia, for her part, has already landed one good blow on those folks inside."

"Landed one good blow... Ah, yeah, that figures. Ain't no way neechan would just take that lyin' down. ...Don't tell me you got caught 'cause of that?"

"No, that's not it. But there's nothing I can do right this moment."

"...This is about Crusch-neechan and Subaru-niichan, ain't it."

After nodding at Ram's reply, Felt clicked her tongue, and Emilia nodded at that.
It seemed she had also heard about Subaru and the others. But come to think of it, the plan today had been to hurry to Priestella with Reinhard's help, of all people.
If neither Emilia's group nor Felt's group showed up for that arrangement, it was only natural for Felt to worry about what had happened.

"Never mind that long-bearded old guy gettin' killed, suspectin' niichan and the others of bein' the culprits is beyond a sick joke."

"You think so too, Felt-chan?"

"'Course I do, what're ya talkin' about? I've owed niichan one ever since some crazy chick with a thing for guts had me in her sights. And in Priestella, I saw the real deal Sin Archbishops, and I was there escortin' 'Wrath' too, y'know? There's no way niichan's chummy with those nutjobs."

"—!"

At Felt's unwavering reply, Emilia once again had to desperately fight the urge to embrace that petite frame.
But, yes. That was it. It wasn't just Emilia and her faction comrades. Felt, from a different faction, understood too. Surely, other people did as well.
Everyone surely understood just how hardworking and earnest Natsuki Subaru was.

"—Emilia! I'm coming too! I'll be confined together with you!"

Just then, the sound of the council chamber door being forcefully thrown open and the voice of a girl rushing out resounded.
As a startled Emilia and the others turned, there came Filol, running over in a fluster with her hair disheveled, on the verge of tears.
She barreled straight into Emilia's chest with the same momentum, crying,

"Th-there's no such thing as such a one-sided inquiry! I protest! I will! I've become a royal selection candidate, after all! Power! Yes, I'll use all the power at my disposal to have Emilia's unjust treatment abolished...!"

"C-Calm down, Filol. You mustn't do that. I'm very happy you feel that way, but doing something like that would cause trouble for you too."

"What kind of friend can't share a muddied name!? I wouldn't mind getting covered in mud with you, Emilia!"

Lifting her face abruptly in Emilia's chest, Filol said it without a moment's hesitation. Blinking in surprise at her intensity, Emilia felt a powerful swell of emotion.
She'd gone to the trouble of holding back from hugging Felt, and then Filol threw herself at her like this, making all that restraint pointless.

Then, as she was being held tight by Emilia, Filol let out an "Ah," noticing Felt scratching her head right beside them.

Come to think of it, the relationship between these two was very complicated.
Normally, this is where Emilia would have to mediate, but—,

"—Don't worry 'bout a thing, Emilia-neechan. You just worry your head about niichan and the rest for now. No need to take on my problems too."

"Y-Yes, I think that's for the best. I was just about to say the same thing. My, it seems we're very much alike!"

"Well, we might end up fightin' over a single seat twice. Compatible or not, we've sure got a connection, that's for sure."

With one eye closed, Felt looked at Filol with curiosity, while Filol, flustered, looked back at Felt while clinging to Emilia.

There was the matter between these two, of course, and worrying about Subaru and Crusch, and also about Otto and the others who had reportedly bolted from the royal guesthouse—it was nothing but worries.

"I want to believe everyone will be alright..."

"...Indeed. By the way, Lady Felt, a consultation, if I may."

"Huh? What's up, maid-neechan?"

"Earlier, you mentioned you owe Barusu a debt. Would you care to repay it sooner rather than later?"

"Huh?"

At Ram's words, Felt raised one eyebrow, a grin of interest twisting her cheek.
At Felt's reaction and Ram's attitude, Emilia realized, "Could it be..." If it was about repaying a favor to Subaru—,

"—Is the 'Sword Saint' with you today?"

"Well, yeah, figured you'd ask that. This whole situation's makin' me sick. I ain't about to just sit back, and I'd happily lend him out... is what I'd like to say."

"...It sounds difficult?"

"Nah, he got called to a different part of the castle just now for some other matter. Same as me."

As Felt answered, scratching her head roughly, Emilia exchanged a glance with Ram. Then, timidly, Filol, still in Emilia's arms, tilted her head,

"Same as you... you were called here too? Not just because you were worried about Emilia?"

"It ain't *just* worry. My bad."

"That's not bad at all, but being summoned..."

"—Me too, to that room."

Saying that, Felt jerked her chin to indicate the room Filol had burst out of, the room where Emilia had undergone her inquiry—the council chamber.

Looking around, the soldiers surrounding Emilia's group as they stopped in the hallway included not only those there to escort Emilia and Ram, but also soldiers guiding Felt. The circumstances were likely different from Emilia and Ram being taken away by Knight Commander Marcos, but—,

"Dragon or Witch, whichever shows up—ain't a good feelin' either way, right?"

Faced with Felt's characteristic grin, the fact that she couldn't feel the same reassurance as always was something that frustrated Emilia terribly.

