—Around that same time, Reinhard van Astrea, summoned to a separate room in the royal castle, was looking down at a map of the royal capital spread out on a table.

"—"

In the center of the map was placed a piece representing the royal guesthouse located in the noble district.
Numerous routes extending from there to the outskirts of the noble district were marked with red indicators. The familiar layout of the royal capital, however, had now transformed into a cold diagram showing escape routes and containment lines.
And what that signified was—,

"It is presumed that the remaining members of Lady Emilia's faction who departed the royal guesthouse slipped through the surveillance net and are plotting a means to escape beyond the noble district."

The one who gave that report was a civil official dispatched as a messenger from the "Council of Elders."
With a blank expression and tone devoid of emotion, an attitude thoroughly dedicated to fulfilling his assigned role—Reinhard made no comment. He merely listened to the reason he had been summoned.

"—"

"The objective of these individuals is suspected to be either meeting up with the knight Natsuki Subaru, or preparing to recover Lady Emilia, who remains within the castle. Naturally, this is merely conjecture at present, but the fact that they exploited a fire disturbance to leave the guesthouse placed under surveillance is a serious matter."

"A fire?"

"Smoke rose from beneath the kitchen floor, it is said. The spread of actual fire was not confirmed, and the majority of the smoke was due to poor ventilation caused by a blocked chimney."

"I see."

Revealing the circumstances by which the watch soldiers had been deceived, the civil official turned a page of the written orders in his hand. Looking in turn at the orders and the map on the table,

"We are in pursuit, but the individuals in question possess extraordinary abilities. Should we rush to suppress them, there is a risk of casualties on both the soldiers' side and the targets' side. Therefore—"

"—A command has been given to me."

"Yes. Sir Reinhard van Astrea, the 'Sword Saint,' you have been ordered to pursue and apprehend them. Here are the orders."

With that, the written orders handed over were indeed inscribed, word for word, with exactly the same content the civil official had just conveyed, making the rigidity of that thorough stance plainly felt.

"—"

Normally, Reinhard would have instantly accepted the contents of a written order his eyes had scanned and moved into action.
However, at this moment, the 'Sword Saint's' reply was slightly delayed. That was not unrelated to the presence of the liege who had accompanied Reinhard to the royal castle—,

"—Valga Cromwell."

Abruptly, the name the civil official uttered lowered the temperature of the small room's air by a degree.

"—"

A name. The civil official spoke only that, offering no further words. And from Reinhard's side as well, no words to question its meaning were issued.
After a brief silence, Reinhard folded the written orders and returned them to the civil official.
And then—,

"—Understood."

Saying only that, Reinhard averted his gaze from both the map and the civil official.
As he turned on his heel, the civil official added a single word to his back.

"The targets are to be apprehended."

"I will stop them."

—Leaving only that single sentence behind, the 'Sword Saint' departed the small conference room of the royal castle.











